No build, configure, lint, export or device operation has been run by this prep.
The earlier 24-seed proposal is untouched. The canonical integration must first
be reviewed, qualified and committed with a completely clean index/worktree.
The original revision is preserved byte-for-byte in history/revision01 (63
files), including campaign.py SHA32e2ecb190663468f8a74d647b1a9e436ae0410ccaa06b5ba64f1d0caaa192b0.
The live revision uses schema v2 and plan02. Historical plan01/reports are never
overwritten. Preparation-only guard_checks.py exercises copied fixtures, never
the committed baselines, SDK files or a production build directory.

`campaign.py plan` snapshots the six complete committed early-MPI firmware
baselines, their raw Git blobs/LFS pointers and hydrated payload identities.
Seven immutable seeds change only YORADIO_TLS_STATIC_RX_RESERVE. The six enabled
rows keep reserve/reclaim/MPI true across vendor/custom FLAC and all three
backends. The disabled vendor PDM control starts from early-mpi-pdm, with
reclaim/MPI still true. No seed uses a mutable project sdkconfig or MPI-off image.

Successful app exports go to NEW firmware/development/esp32-cyd2usb-native-static-rx-*
directories through the existing production exporter. Existing/versioned
artifacts are not writable destinations. Six independent ON Clang configs use
fresh short build directories and run_native_lint.py with every project-owned
unit and both HTTPD overlays. The actual TLS SDK overlay receives its own real
Clang frontend/dependency-closure check; the normal lint filter excludes it.
No warning suppression is added. Parser errors fail; warnings remain visible
for root triage and are not a clean-code claim.

