Qualification covers actual source/config/compiler/SDK/OTA provenance, original
board and task calls/profiles, exact SSL patch and consumed headers, registry
init/free hooks, zero userdata access in the canonical module, static/internal
full RX storage, ordinary allocator/free pointers and reserve-off absence.
The later export qualifier compiles one isolated, unlinked SDK sizeof-array
probe with the actual module flags and requires its MBEDTLS_SSL_IN_BUFFER_LEN
size to equal the linked s_rx size. No numerical overhead constant is guessed.
The freeze marker explicitly records Git, bootstrap/SDK Python, PowerShell,
CMake/Ninja, GCC drivers/binutils/private helpers, Clang tools and the invoked
repository/SDK Python/PowerShell entry scripts. Actual selected compiler rows
and generated CMake Python/generator selections must match those identities.
Preparation's argv proof stores an existing real Clang command unchanged, its
Windows CommandLineToArgvW argv and serialization roundtrip, including quoted
macro values. It invokes no compiler. All saved lint logs/YAML and consumed
headers/objects are rehashed when the matrix closes.
Actual ELF/map section sizes and app/OTA sizes are recorded against each frozen
baseline. Only new vendor PDM ON/OFF is a same-commit controlled comparison;
other baseline comparisons span source commits and are labelled accordingly.
Neither lower allocation count nor section deltas prove heap/resource savings.
Physical TLS/HTTP, playback, concurrent WebUI/OTA and memory/stack measurements
remain open. No deferred decoder extension or private owner investigation runs.

